# Build, commit, and push

When you finish implementing requested code changes in this repo:

1. Run the relevant build (`npm run build` for the mini-app) and fix errors until it passes.
2. Commit all related changes (never commit `.env` or other secrets unless the user explicitly asks).
3. Push to `origin` on the current branch without waiting for the user to ask.

Skip commit/push only when the user explicitly says not to, or when the task was question-only / no code changes.
